    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0834" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9499</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received April 12, 10.35 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As yet threatened destruction of cable station by submarine has not been
                    attempted. Submarine not seen since about 7 last evening. Liberian Government
                    vessel, named <hi rendition="#italic">President
                    Howard</hi>, sunk yesterday by submarine. Result of running
                    fight yesterday in view of Monrovia between merchant steamer and submarine
                    obscured by darkness. No casualties among foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
